Alsayf imports the pinned upstream WinRM/WinRS client, SOAP shell and command
lifecycle, response parsing, NTLM authentication and message encryption, and
PowerShell command encoding. Upstream runtime sources are not modified or copied.

The cmd/winrm and internal/winrm adapters provide CLI commands, password sources,
TLS options, socket-bound cancellation and timeouts, SOAP fault handling,
stream/error propagation, UTF-8 PowerShell input, and bounded shell cleanup.
Authentication exposed by this adapter is NTLM or Basic over HTTPS. Kerberos,
CredSSP, certificate authentication, and PSRP runspaces are not exposed.

No Evil-WinRM code, Ruby interpreter, external client executable, or Windows
server components are bundled. The remote Windows WinRM service must already
be configured; Alsayf does not change its authentication or firewall settings.
